## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical performance planning skills for ML inference services with batching, autoscaling, and cache effects in real-world production deployments.

## Key Concepts
- Tail latency under batching and its impact on P99/P999 percentiles
- Batch window vs. throughput trade-offs: larger windows increase throughput but add latency
- Observability: metrics, traces, and dashboards for end-to-end visibility
- Autoscaling triggers: latency thresholds, queue depth, and custom metrics
- Failure modes: GPU memory pressure, OOM kills, batcher stalls, and throttling

## Code Example
```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';

export const options = {
  stages: [
    { duration: '60s', target: 100 },   // Warm-up
    { duration: '120s', target: 500 },  // 5x burst
  ],
  thresholds: {
    http_req_duration: ['p(99)<500'],    // P99 < 500ms
    http_reqs: ['rate>1000'],            // >1000 RPS
  },
};

export default function () {
  const res = http.post('https://inference.service/predict', 
    JSON.stringify({ input: 'data' }),
    { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } }
  );
  check(res, { 'status is 200': (r) => r.status === 200 });
  sleep(Math.random() * 0.1);  // Random inter-arrival
}
```

## Workload Model
| Parameter | Cold Cache | Warm Cache |
|-----------|------------|------------|
| Request Rate | 100-500 RPS | 100-500 RPS |
| Burst Factor | 3x-5x | 3x-5x |
| Batch Window | 10-100ms | 10-100ms |

## Acceptance Criteria
- P99 latency < 500ms under 5x burst with warm cache
- Autoscaling responds within 60 seconds of traffic spike
- Zero failed requests during burst (error rate < 0.1%)
- Throughput scales linearly with batch size up to GPU memory limit

